I'm just like super-busy right now, so...
/aɪm ˈdʒʌst ˈlaɪk ˈsuˈːpɚbɪzi ˈraɪt ˈnaʊ ˈsoʊ/

140
00:07:19,702 --> 00:07:23,295
maybe we should just... call it a day.
/ˈmeɪbiː wiː ˌʃʊd ˈdʒʌst ˈkɔːl ɪɾ ɐ ˈdeɪ/

141
00:07:24,444 --> 00:07:26,387
But you're awesome.
/ˌbʌt jʊr ˈɔːsʌm/

142
00:07:26,387 --> 00:07:28,826
On her answering machine!?
/ˌɑːn hɜːr ˈænsɚrɪŋ məˈʃiːn/

143
00:07:28,826 --> 00:07:31,089
- And on her birthday?!
- Lily, come on.

144
00:07:31,089 --> 00:07:35,873
Oh, who breaks up with somebody on their answering machine on her birthday?!
/ˈoʊ ˌhuː ˈbreɪks ˌʌp wɪð ˈsʌmbɑːdi ˌɑːn ðɛr ˈænsɚrɪŋ məˈʃiːn ˌɑːn hɜː ˈbɜːθdeɪ/

145
00:07:35,873 --> 00:07:37,756
Yeah, dude. E-mail.
/ˈjɛh ˈduːd ˈiˈːmeɪl/

146
00:07:38,112 --> 00:07:41,338
Not exactly the point I was trying to make, Marshall.
/ˌnɑːt ɛˈɡzæktli ðə ˈpɔɪnt aɪ wʌz ˈtraɪɪŋ tə ˈmeɪk ˈmɑːrʃəl/

147
00:07:41,338 --> 00:07:44,258
That is a terrible way to break up with someone.
/ðæt ɪz ɐ ˈtɛrəbəl ˈweɪ tə ˈbreɪk ˌʌp wɪð ˈsʌmwʌn/

148
