Okay, in my client's defense,
/oʊˈkeɪ ɪn maɪ ˈklaɪənts dɪˈfɛns/

149
00:07:45,770 --> 00:07:48,725
is there an unterrible way to break up with somebody? No.
/ɪz ðɛr ɐn ʌˈntɛrəbəl ˈweɪ tə ˈbreɪk ˌʌp wɪð ˈsʌmbɑːdi ˈnoʊ/

150
00:07:48,725 --> 00:07:53,248
Personally, I'd rather hear the bad news on an answering machine than face the humiliation in person.
/ˈpɜːsənəli aɪd ˈræðɚ ˈhɪr ðə ˈbæd ˈnuːz ˌɑːn ɐn ˈænsɚrɪŋ məˈʃiːn ðɐn ˈfeɪs ðə ˌhjuːmɪlɪˈeɪʃən ɪn ˈpɜːsən/

151
00:07:53,248 --> 00:07:55,248
It's the least painful way you can do it.
/ɪts ðə ˈliːst ˈpeɪnfəl ˈweɪ juː kæn ˈduː ɪt/

152
00:07:55,248 --> 00:07:57,486
- Who are you calling?
- Hi, Marshall, it Lily.

153
00:07:57,486 --> 00:08:01,086
We're not gonna have sex for at least a month, but you're awesome.
/wɪr ˌnɑːt ˌɡənə hæv ˈsɛks fɔːr æt ˈliːst ɐ ˈmʌnθ ˌbʌt jʊr ˈɔːsʌm/

154
00:08:01,086 --> 00:08:02,419
Okay, bye-bye.
/oʊˈkeɪ ˈbaɪˈbaɪ/

155
00:08:03,039 --> 00:08:06,191
No, that was a big mistake, Ted.
/ˈnoʊ ðæt wʌzɐ ˈbɪɡ mɪˈsteɪk ˈtɛd/
You should've done it in person.
/juː ˌʃʊdəv ˈdʌn ɪɾ ɪn ˈpɜːsən/

156
00:08:06,191 --> 00:08:07,287
Thank you.
/ˈθæŋk juː/

157
00:08:07,287 --> 00:08:10,954
Desperate, please-don't-leave-me sex is amazing.
/ˈdɛspɚrət ˈpliˈːzdoʊˈntliˌːvmiː ˈsɛks ɪz ɐˈmeɪzɪŋ/

158
00:08:11,535 --> 00:08:14,155
Okay, it was childish and stupid.
/oʊˈkeɪ ɪt wʌz ˈtʃaɪldɪʃ ænd ˈstuːpɪd/
I just...
/aɪ ˈdʒʌst/

159
00:08:14,155 --> 00:08:15,472
I didn't want to see her cry.
/aɪ ˈdɪdnt ˈwɑːnt tə ˈsiː hɜː ˈkraɪ/

160
00:08:15,472 --> 00:08:18,187
Well, guess what?
/ˈwɛl ˈɡɛs ˈwʌt/
She cried.
/ʃiː ˈkraɪd/

161
00:08:18,187 --> 00:08:20,915
You just didn't have the sack to face those tears.
/juː ˈdʒʌst ˈdɪdnt hæv ðə ˈsæk tə ˈfeɪs ðoʊz ˈtɪrz/

162
00:08:20,915 --> 00:08:22,432
That was me then, okay?
/ðæt wʌz ˌmiː ˈðɛn oʊˈkeɪ/

163
00:08:22,432 --> 00:08:25,803
This is the new, old-shirt- wearing, sack-having Ted.
