164
00:08:25,803 --> 00:08:27,155
I'm gonna make this right.
/aɪm ˌɡənə ˌmeɪk ðɪs ˈraɪt/

165
00:08:27,155 --> 00:08:27,850
You know what else?
/juː ˈnoʊ wʌt ˈɛls/

166
00:08:27,850 --> 00:08:30,800
"My younger sister just got married and I'm about to turn 30" sex.
/maɪ ˈjʌŋɡɚ ˈsɪstɚ ˈdʒʌst ɡɑːt ˈmærid ænd aɪm ɐˌbaʊt tə ˈtɜːn ˈθɜːɾi ˈsɛks/

167
00:08:30,800 --> 00:08:32,843
Fantastic.
/fæˈntæstɪk/

168
00:08:34,281 --> 00:08:36,605
An occasion that was supposed to be joyous,
/ɐn əˈkeɪʒən ðæt wʌz sʌˈpoʊzd təbi ˈdʒɔɪəs/

169
00:08:36,605 --> 00:08:39,770
suddenly turned tragic when Ethel and Sadie Margolis,
/ˈsʌdənli ˈtɜːnd ˈtrædʒɪk wɛn ˈɛθəl ænd ˈseɪdi ˈmɑːrɡɑːliz/

170
00:08:39,770 --> 00:08:43,608
New York's oldest twins, suddenly passed away on this,
/ˈnuː ˈjɔːrks ˈoʊldəst ˈtwɪnz ˈsʌdənli ˈpæst ɐˈweɪ ˌɑːn ˈðɪs/

171
00:08:43,608 --> 00:08:46,482
the eve of their 100th birthday.
/ðɪ ˈiːv ʌv ðɛr ˈwʌˈnhʌndrəd θ ˈbɜːθdeɪ/

172
00:08:46,482 --> 00:08:49,262
I'm a dirty, dirty girl.
/aɪm ɐ ˈdɜːɾi ˈdɜːɾi ˈɡɜːl/

173
00:08:51,300 --> 00:08:55,131
Reporting live, Robin Trubotsky, Metro News One.
/rɪˈpoːrɾɪŋ ˈlaɪv ˈrɑːbɪn truˈːbɑːtski ˈmɛtroʊ ˈnuːz ˌwʌn/

174
00:08:55,131 --> 00:08:56,402
Clear.
/ˈklɪr/

175
00:08:57,550 --> 00:09:01,353
Joel Adams wants to see you in his office.
/ˈdʒoʊl ˈædəmz ˈwɑːnts tə ˈsiː juː ɪn hɪz ˈɑːfɪs/

176
00:09:02,400 --> 00:09:03,683
Before you say anything,
/bɪˌfoːr juː ˈseɪ ˈɛnɪˌθɪŋ/

177
00:09:03,683 --> 00:09:07,235
I just want to say I really like working here at Metro News One.
/aɪ ˈdʒʌst ˈwɑːnt tə ˈseɪ aɪ ˈriəli ˈlaɪk ˈwɜːkɪŋ ˈhɪr æt ˈmɛtroʊ ˈnuːz ˌwʌn/

178
00:09:07,235 --> 00:09:13,033
- That's great.
- So, my dog keeps going...

179
00:09:14,300 --> 00:09:16,557
- What's...?
- What? You have dogs, right?

180
00:09:16,557 --> 00:09:18,144
What do you think that means?
/ˌwʌt ˈduː juː ˈθɪŋk ðæt ˈmiːnz/

181
00:09:18,144 --> 00:09:20,398
Take him to the vet?
/ˈteɪk ˌhɪm tə ðə ˈvɛt/

182
00:09:20,989 --> 00:09:22,376
Genius.
/ˈdʒiːnɪəs/

183
00:09:22,376 --> 00:09:24,249
That's one I owe you.
/ðæts ˈwʌn aɪ ˈoʊ juː/

184
00:09:24,600 --> 00:09:27,139
- Was that all?
- Yeah.

185
00:09:29,400 --> 00:09:30,904
And nothing about the twins story?
/ænd ˈnʌθɪŋ ɐˌbaʊt ðə ˈtwɪnz ˈstoːri/

186
00:09:30,904 --> 00:09:32,499
Oh, yeah, great job on that one.
/ˈoʊ ˈjɛh ˈɡreɪt ˈdʒɑːb ˌɑːn ˈðæˌtwʌn/

187
00:09:32,499 --> 00:09:35,545
New York loves you. You're a superstar. Bye-bye.
/ˈnuː ˈjɔːrk ˈlʌvz juː jʊr ɐ ˈsuˌːpɚstɑːr ˈbaɪˈbaɪ/

188
00:09:36,937 --> 00:09:42,308
That's when Robin realized that no one, not even her boss, watched Metro News One.
/ðæts wɛn ˈrɑːbɪn ˈriːəlaɪzd ðæt ˈnoʊˈwʌn ˌnɑːt ˈiːvən hɜː ˈbɔs ˈwɑːtʃt ˈmɛtroʊ ˈnuːz ˌwʌn/

189
00:09:56,400 --> 00:09:59,540
Natalie! Come on!
/ˈnæɾɐli ˈkʌm ˈɑːn/
I just want to say I'm sorry.
/aɪ ˈdʒʌst ˈwɑːnt tə ˈseɪ aɪm ˈsɔːri/

190
00:09:59,540 --> 00:10:01,858
I only came down here 'cause you wouldn't take my call.
/aɪ ˈoʊnli ˈkeɪm ˌdaʊn ˈhɪr ˈkɔːz juː ˈwʊdənt ˈteɪk maɪ ˈkɔːl/

191
00:10:01,858 --> 00:10:03,406
Hey, here's an idea--
/ˈheɪ ˈhɪrz ɐn aɪˈdiə/

192
00:10:03,406 --> 00:10:05,761
Why don't you leave a message?
/ˌwaɪ ˈdoʊnt juː ˈliːv ɐ ˈmɛsɪdʒ/

193
00:10:07,446 --> 00:10:08,658
Good one.
/ˈɡʊd ˌwʌn/

194
00:10:08,658 --> 00:10:12,284
Okay, fine, I'm just going to leave this sock monkey here.
/oʊˈkeɪ ˈfaɪn aɪm ˈdʒʌst ˌɡoʊɪŋ tə ˈliːv ðɪs ˈsɑːk ˈmʌnki ˈhɪr/

195
00:10:12,284 --> 00:10:14,338
Good-bye.
/ˈɡʊˈdbaɪ/

196
00:10:19,800 --> 00:10:21,116
Look, look, look.
/ˈlʊk ˈlʊk ˈlʊk/

197
00:10:21,116 --> 00:10:24,316
I know you're mad, but... happy birthday.
/aɪ ˈnoʊ jʊr ˈmæd ˈbʌt ˈhæpi ˈbɜːθdeɪ/

198
00:10:24,316 --> 00:10:26,449
- Three years ago.
- Oh, yeah?

199
00:10:26,449 --> 00:10:28,415
Up yours three years ago.
/ˌʌp ˈjoːrz ˈθriː ˈjɪrz ɐˈɡoʊ/

200
00:10:28,415 --> 00:10:31,429
Look, look, I was an idiot leaving that message.
/ˈlʊk ˈlʊk aɪ wʌz ɐn ˈɪdɪət ˈliːvɪŋ ðæt ˈmɛsɪdʒ/

201
00:10:31,429 --> 00:10:33,432
I realize how much that sucked.
/aɪ ˈriːəlaɪz ˌhaʊ ˈmʌtʃ ðæt ˈsʌkt/

202
00:10:33,731 --> 00:10:35,529
No, you don't.
/ˈnoʊ juː ˈdoʊnt/

203
00:10:35,529 --> 00:10:38,663
Maybe we should just call it a day.
/ˈmeɪbiː wiː ˌʃʊd ˈdʒʌst ˈkɔːl ɪɾ ɐ ˈdeɪ/

204
00:10:39,144 --> 00:10:42,068
But you're awesome.
/ˌbʌt jʊr ˈɔːsʌm/

205
00:10:42,809 --> 00:10:44,923
Okay, bye.
/oʊˈkeɪ ˈbaɪ/

206
00:10:47,200 --> 00:10:49,067
Surprise.
/ˈsɚpraɪz/

207
00:10:50,387 --> 00:10:52,696
There was a surprise party that night?
/ðɛˌrwʌz ɐ ˈsɚpraɪz ˈpɑːrɾi ðæt ˈnaɪt/

208
00:10:52,696 --> 00:10:54,233
How come nobody told me?
/ˌhaʊ ˈkʌm ˈnoʊbɑːdi ˈtoʊld ˌmiː/

209
00:10:54,233 --> 00:10:57,467
People think I can't keep a secret, but I totally can.
/ˈpiːpəl ˈθɪŋk aɪ ˈkænt ˈkiːp ɐ ˈsiːkrət ˌbʌt aɪ ˈtoʊɾəli ˈkæn/

210
00:10:58,018 --> 00:10:59,700
Sorry, not the issue.
/ˈsɔːri ˌnɑːt ðɪ ˈɪʃuː/

211
00:10:59,700 --> 00:11:03,852
Look, Natalie, I was just a stupid kid back then, terrified of commitment.
/ˈlʊk ˈnæɾɐli aɪ wʌz ˈdʒʌst ɐ ˈstuːpɪd ˈkɪd ˈbæk ˈðɛn ˈtɛˌrᵻfaɪd ʌv kəˈmɪtmənt/

212
00:11:03,852 --> 00:11:07,202
And I suppose you're suddenly ready to get married and settle down.
/ænd aɪ sʌˈpoʊz jʊr ˈsʌdənli ˈrɛdi tə ɡɛt ˈmærid ænd ˈsɛɾəl ˈdaʊn/

213
00:11:07,532 --> 00:11:09,425
Well, yeah, actually.
/ˈwɛl ˈjɛh ˈæktʃuːəli/

214
00:11:09,800 --> 00:11:11,522
I'm a different guy now.
/aɪm ɐ ˈdɪfrənt ˈɡaɪ ˈnaʊ/

215
00:11:12,427 --> 00:11:14,164
Give me another chance, huh?
/ˈɡɪv ˌmiː ɐˈnʌðɚ ˈtʃæns ˈhʌ/

216
00:11:14,164 --> 00:11:17,263
You must think I have absolutely no self-respect.
/juː ˈmʌst ˈθɪŋk aɪ hæv ˌæbsəˈluːtli ˈnoʊ ˈsɛlfrɪˈspɛkt/

217
00:11:17,263 --> 00:11:19,937
Come on, just a cup of coffee.
/ˈkʌm ˈɑːn ˈdʒʌst ɐ ˈkʌp ʌv ˈkɔfi/

218
00:11:21,750 --> 00:11:25,239
Please, Natalie.
/ˈpliːz ˈnæɾɐli/
Give the guy a chance.
/ˈɡɪv ðə ˈɡaɪ ɐ ˈtʃæns/

219
00:11:25,613 --> 00:11:28,388
Self-respect is overrated.
/ˈsɛlfrɪˈspɛkt ɪz ˌoʊˈvɚreɪɾᵻd/

220
00:11:36,600 --> 00:11:40,351
Maybe it was the caffeine, but you really brought your game up to a whole new level.
/ˈmeɪbiː ɪt wʌzðə kæˈfiːn ˌbʌt juː ˈriəli ˈbrɔːt jʊr ˈɡeɪm ˌʌp tʊ ɐ ˈhoʊl ˈnuː ˈlɛvəl/

221
00:11:40,351 --> 00:11:41,482
Thanks.
/ˈθæŋks/

222
00:11:41,482 --> 00:11:43,836
I did just start subscribing to Esquire.
/aɪ ˈdɪd ˈdʒʌst ˈstɑːrt səˈbskraɪbɪŋ tʊ ɛˈskwaɪɚ/

223
00:11:43,836 --> 00:11:45,593
They have some helpful columns.
/ðeɪ hæv ˌsʌm ˈhɛlpfəl ˈkɑːlʌmz/

224
00:11:45,900 --> 00:11:49,924
The following is from the October issue.
/ðə ˈfɑːloʊɪŋ ɪz frʌmðɪ ɑˈːktoʊbɚr ˈɪʃuː/

225
00:11:51,113 --> 00:11:53,340
So Natalie and I started dating again.
/ˌsoʊ ˈnæɾɐli ænd aɪ ˈstɑːrɾᵻd ˈdeɪɾɪŋ ɐˈɡɛn/

226
00:11:53,340 --> 00:11:55,750
And just like that, it all came back.
/ænd ˈdʒʌst ˈlaɪk ˈðæt ɪɾ ˈɔːl ˈkeɪm ˈbæk/

227
00:11:55,750 --> 00:11:58,914
The tea candles... the sock monkeys...
/ðə ˈtiː ˈkændəlz ðə ˈsɑːk ˈmʌnkiz/

228
00:11:58,914 --> 00:12:01,497
Belle and Sebastian, all of it.
/ˈbɛl ænd səˈbæstʃən ˈɔːl ʌv ɪt/

229
00:12:01,497 --> 00:12:04,778
It seemed like happily ever after wasn't far off.
/ɪt ˈsiːmd ˈlaɪk ˈhæpɪli ˈɛvɚr ˈæftɚ ˈwʌzn̩t ˈfɑːr ˈɔf/

230
00:12:05,148 --> 00:12:08,061
Well, I better run.
/ˈwɛl aɪ ˈbɛɾɚ ˈrʌn/
I have my Krav Maga class in half an hour.
/aɪ hæv maɪ ˈkræv ˈmɑːɡə ˈklæs ɪn ˈhæf ɐn ˈaɪʊr/

231
00:12:08,061 --> 00:12:11,404
Krav Maga. How cool is it that she does Krav Maga?
/ˈkræv ˈmɑːɡə ˌhaʊ ˈkuːl ɪz ɪt ðæt ʃiː ˈdʌz ˈkræv ˈmɑːɡə/

232
00:12:11,404 --> 00:12:13,036
Thanks, honey.
/ˈθæŋks ˈhʌni/

233
00:12:14,112 --> 00:12:16,741
- Bye, guys.
- Bye!
- Take it easy.

234
00:12:17,400 --> 00:12:19,257
Dude, what's Krav Maga?
/ˈduːd ˌwʌts ˈkræv ˈmɑːɡə/

235
00:12:19,257 --> 00:12:21,703
I have no idea.
/aɪ hæv ˈnoʊ aɪˈdiə/
Some kind of yoga?
/ˌsʌm ˈkaɪnd ʌv ˈjoʊɡə/

236
00:12:22,600 --> 00:12:24,531
You know, that Natalie, she's good times.
/juː ˈnoʊ ðæt ˈnæɾɐli ʃiːz ˈɡʊd ˈtaɪmz/

237
00:12:24,531 --> 00:12:26,458
Yeah, she's, like, the best girl you've dated in years.
/ˈjɛh ˈʃiːz ˈlaɪk ðə ˈbɛst ˈɡɜːl juːv ˈdeɪɾᵻd ɪn ˈjɪrz/

238
00:12:26,458 --> 00:12:28,952
- Yeah, Ted, hold on to that one.
- Yeah.

239
00:12:28,952 --> 00:12:31,279
I have to break up with her.
/aɪ hæv tə ˈbreɪk ˈʌp wɪð hɜː/

240
00:12:35,900 --> 00:12:38,494
I don't get it, man.
/aɪ ˈdoʊnt ˈɡɛt ɪt ˈmæn/
Natalie's awesome.
/ˈnæɾɐliz ˈɔːsʌm/

241
00:12:38,494 --> 00:12:41,800
I know, she's terrific, but I have to break up with her.
/aɪ ˈnoʊ ʃiːz ˈtɚrɪfɪk ˌbʌt aɪ hæv tə ˈbreɪk ˈʌp wɪð hɜː/

242
00:12:42,987 --> 00:12:46,427
Why couldn't you leave that poor girl alone?
/ˌwaɪ ˌkʊdənt juː ˈliːv ðæt ˈpʊr ˈɡɜːl ɐˈloʊn/

243
00:12:46,427 --> 00:12:47,958
I know. I hate this.
/aɪ ˈnoʊ aɪ ˈheɪt ˈðɪs/

244
00:12:47,958 --> 00:12:49,588
These past three weeks have been great.
/ðiːz ˈpæst ˈθriː ˈwiːks hɐvbɪn ˈɡreɪt/

245
00:12:49,588 --> 00:12:53,093
I should be in love with her, but I'm not feeling that thing.
/aɪ ˌʃʊd biː ɪn ˈlʌv wɪð hɜː ˌbʌt aɪm ˌnɑːt ˈfiːlɪŋ ðæt ˈθɪŋ/

246
00:12:53,093 --> 00:12:56,439
- It's ineffable.
- Ineffable.

247
00:12:56,439 --> 00:12:57,701
Good word.
/ˈɡʊd ˈwɜːd/

248
00:12:58,004 --> 00:12:59,476
So when are you going to do it?
/ˌsoʊ wɛn ɑːr juː ˌɡoʊɪŋ tə ˈduː ɪt/

249
00:12:59,476 --> 00:13:00,962
She's probably on the subway by now.
/ʃiːz ˈprɑːbəbli ɑːnðə ˈsʌbweɪ baɪ ˈnaʊ/

250
00:13:00,962 --> 00:13:02,346
You could call her voice mail:
/juː kʊd ˈkɔːl hɜː ˈvɔɪs ˈmeɪl/

251
00:13:02,346 --> 00:13:04,992
Beep! "Dumped."
/ˈbiːp ˈdʌmpt/
Click. Done.
/ˈklɪk ˈdʌn/

252
00:13:05,937 --> 00:13:07,712
No, I have to do this face-to-face.
/ˈnoʊ aɪ hæv tə ˈduː ðɪs ˈfeɪstəˈfeɪs/

253
00:13:07,712 --> 00:13:09,223
I just, I don't know what I'm going to say.
/aɪ ˈdʒʌst aɪ ˈdoʊnt ˈnoʊ wʌt aɪm ˌɡoʊɪŋ tə ˈseɪ/

254
00:13:09,223 --> 00:13:11,246
"I'm not ready for a commitment."
/aɪm ˌnɑːt ˈrɛdi fɚrə kəˈmɪtmənt/

255
00:13:11,246 --> 00:13:14,853
- Oh, that's such a cliché.
- It's not a cliché, it's a classic.

256
00:13:15,127 --> 00:13:17,472
It's the "Stairway to Heaven" of breakup lines.
/ɪts ðə ˈstɛrweɪ tə ˈhɛvən ʌv ˈbreɪkʌp ˈlaɪnz/

257
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:20,306
Well, I think Natalie deserves better.
/ˈwɛl aɪ ˈθɪŋk ˈnæɾɐli dɪˈzɜːvz ˈbɛɾɚ/

258
00:13:20,306 --> 00:13:23,055
Better. There's no "better" in breaking up.
/ˈbɛɾɚ ðɛrz ˈnoʊ ˈbɛɾɚ ɪn ˈbreɪkɪŋ ˈʌp/

259
00:13:23,055 --> 00:13:26,817
There's only "less awful."
/ðɛrz ˈoʊnli ˈlɛs ˈɔːfəl/
A cliché is a cliché for a reason.
/ɐ klɪˈʃeɪ ɪz ɐ klɪˈʃeɪ fɚrɚ ˈriːzən/

260
00:13:27,227 --> 00:13:28,765
- It's comforting.
- It doesn't matter.

261
00:13:28,765 --> 00:13:31,500
I already told her I am ready for a commitment, so...
/aɪ ɔˌːlrɛdi ˈtoʊld hɜːr aɪɐm ˈrɛdi fɚrə kəˈmɪtmənt ˈsoʊ/

262
00:13:31,500 --> 00:13:34,441
Oh, my God. There's no way out.
/ˈoʊ maɪ ˈɡɑːd ðɛrz ˈnoʊ ˈweɪ ˈaʊt/
I'm gonna have to marry her.
/aɪm ˌɡənə hæv tə ˈmæri hɜː/

263
00:13:34,441 --> 00:13:36,755
No, no, we're gonna get you out of this.
/ˈnoʊ ˈnoʊ wɪr ˌɡənə ɡɛt juː ˌaʊɾəv ˈðɪs/

264
00:13:36,755 --> 00:13:40,552
Okay, how about... "It's not you, it's me"?
/oʊˈkeɪ ˌhaʊ ɐˈbaʊt ɪts ˈnɑːt juː ɪts ˈmiː/

265
00:13:40,552 --> 00:13:42,696
Mm, mm, six words--
/ˌɛˈmɛm ˌɛˈmɛm ˈsɪks ˈwɜːdz/

266
00:13:42,696 --> 00:13:45,721
"You look fat in those jeans."
/juː ˈlʊk ˈfæt ɪn ðoʊz ˈdʒiːnz/
You're free to go.
/jʊr ˈfriː tə ˈɡoʊ/

267
00:13:46,773 --> 00:13:49,958
Ted, have you considered telling her the truth?
/ˈtɛd hæv juː kəˈnsɪdɚd ˈtɛlɪŋ hɜː ðə ˈtruːθ/

268
00:13:52,080 --> 00:13:54,484
Seriously, honey, men are working here.
/ˈsiərɪəsli ˈhʌni ˈmɛn ɑːr ˈwɜːkɪŋ ˈhɪr/

269
00:13:54,965 --> 00:13:58,301
Ted, what is the truth?
/ˈtɛd ˌwʌt ɪz ðə ˈtruːθ/
Why do you want to break up with her?
/ˌwaɪ ˈduː juː ˈwɑːnt tə ˈbreɪk ˈʌp wɪð hɜː/

270
00:13:58,301 --> 00:14:00,726
The truth?
/ðə ˈtruːθ/
She's not the one.
/ʃiːz ˌnɑːt ðə ˈwʌn/

271
00:14:00,726 --> 00:14:03,477
- So tell her that.
- Oh, you can't tell her that.

272
00:14:03,477 --> 00:14:04,608
That's horrible.
/ðæts ˈhɔːrɪbəl/

273
00:14:04,608 --> 00:14:07,182
Why? What is so horrible about that?
/ˈwaɪ ˌwʌt ɪz ˌsoʊ ˈhɔːrɪbəl ɐˌbaʊt ˈðæt/

274
00:14:07,182 --> 00:14:10,980
Yeah, what is so horrible about that?
/ˈjɛh ˌwʌt ɪz ˌsoʊ ˈhɔːrɪbəl ɐˌbaʊt ˈðæt/
She's not the one.
/ʃiːz ˌnɑːt ðə ˈwʌn/

275
00:14:10,980 --> 00:14:13,113
Why is that such a heartbreaking thing to hear?
/ˌwaɪ ɪz ðæt ˈsʌtʃ ɐ ˈhɑːrtbreɪkɪŋ ˈθɪŋ tə ˈhɪr/

276
00:14:13,113 --> 00:14:17,483
The chances of one person being another person's "the one" are, like, six billion-to-one.
/ðə ˈtʃænsɪz ʌv ˈwʌn ˈpɜːsən ˌbiːɪŋ ɐˈnʌðɚ ˈpɜːsənz ðə ˈwʌn ɑːr ˈlaɪk ˈsɪks ˈbɪliəntəˌwʌn/

277
00:14:17,483 --> 00:14:20,149
Yeah, you have better chances of winning the lottery.
/ˈjɛh juː hæv ˈbɛɾɚ ˈtʃænsɪz ʌv ˈwɪnɪŋ ðə ˈlɑːɾɚri/

278
00:14:20,149 --> 00:14:21,360
Exactly!
/ɛˈɡzæktli/

279
00:14:21,360 --> 00:14:23,324
You wouldn't take it personally if you lost the lottery.
/juː ˈwʊdənt ˈteɪk ɪt ˈpɜːsənəli ɪf juː ˈlɔst ðə ˈlɑːɾɚri/

280
00:14:23,324 --> 00:14:25,178
All right, man, tell her the truth.
/ˈɔːl ˈraɪt ˈmæn ˈtɛl hɜː ðə ˈtruːθ/

281
00:14:25,178 --> 00:14:26,867
She's gonna cry.
/ʃiːz ˌɡənə ˈkraɪ/

282
00:14:26,867 --> 00:14:30,082
Yeah, and he's gonna sit there and he's gonna take it like a man.
/ˈjɛh ænd hiːz ˌɡənə ˈsɪt ðɛr ænd hiːz ˌɡənə ˈteɪk ɪt ˈlaɪk ɐ ˈmæn/

283
00:14:30,082 --> 00:14:31,856
I have to do the mature thing.
/aɪ hæv tə ˈduː ðə məˈtʃʊr ˈθɪŋ/

284
00:14:31,856 --> 00:14:33,182
Want to talk mature?
/ˈwɑːnt tə ˈtɔːk məˈtʃʊr/

285
00:14:33,182 --> 00:14:37,718
I just wrapped up a live newscast by honking my own boobs.
/aɪ ˈdʒʌst ˈræpt ˌʌp ɐ ˈlaɪv ˈnuːzkæst baɪ ˈhɑːŋkɪŋ maɪ ˈoʊn ˈbuːbz/

286
00:14:38,140 --> 00:14:40,954
And great TV was had by all.
/ænd ˈɡreɪt ˌtiˈːviː wʌz hæd baɪ ˈɔːl/

287
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:45,013
All right, Trubotsky, new challenge, and this one's big.
/ˈɔːl ˈraɪt truˈːbɑːtski ˈnuː ˈtʃælɪndʒ ænd ðɪs ˈwʌnz ˈbɪɡ/

288
00:14:45,013 --> 00:14:47,127
But so is the cash reward.
/ˌbʌt ˌsoʊ ɪz ðə ˈkæʃ rɪˈwɔːrd/

289
00:14:47,127 --> 00:14:50,535
For $1,000-- you heard me--
/fɔːr ˈdɑːlɚ ˈwʌn ˈθaʊzənd juː ˈhɜːd ˌmiː/

290
00:14:50,535 --> 00:14:54,168
all you have to do is get up there on the news and do one of these.
/ˈɔːl juː hæv tə ˈduː ɪz ɡɛt ˌʌp ðɛr ɑːnðə ˈnuːz ænd ˈduː ˈwʌn ʌv ˈðiːz/

291
00:15:01,291 --> 00:15:04,231
- What the hell is that?
- The Ickey Shuffle.

292
00:15:04,231 --> 00:15:06,596
And as you do it, you say this:
/ænd æz juː ˈduː ɪt juː ˈseɪ ˈðɪs/

293
00:15:06,596 --> 00:15:11,176
Elbert "Icky" Woods, the Bengals were fools to cut you in '91.
/ˈɛlbɚt ˈaɪki ˈwʊdz ðə ˌbɛˈnɡɔːlz wɜː ˈfuːlz tə ˈkʌt juː ɪn ˈnaɪnti ˈwʌn/

294
00:15:11,176 --> 00:15:15,776
Your 1,525 rushing yards and your 27 touchdowns will not be forgotten.
/jʊr ˈwʌn ˈθaʊzənd ˈfaɪˈvhʌndrəd ˈtwɛnti ˈfaɪv ˈrʌʃɪŋ ˈjɑːrdz ænd jʊr ˈtwɛnti ˈsɛvən ˈtʌtʃdaʊnz wɪl ˌnɑːt biː ˈfɚɡɑːʔn̩/

295
00:15:15,776 --> 00:15:20,722
So Coach Dave Shula, screw you and your crappy steakhouse.
/ˌsoʊ ˈkoʊtʃ ˈdeɪv ˈʃjʊlə ˈskruː juː ænd jʊr ˈkræpi ˈsteɪkhaʊs/

296
00:15:21,913 --> 00:15:24,097
Just write it down for me.
/ˈdʒʌst ˈraɪt ɪt ˈdaʊn fɔːr ˌmiː/

297
00:15:24,447 --> 00:15:25,078
What do I care?
/ˌwʌt ˈduː aɪ ˈkɛr/

298
00:15:25,078 --> 00:15:26,962
It's not like anyone's watching, anyway, right?
/ɪts ˌnɑːt ˈlaɪk ˈɛnɪˌwʌnz ˈwɑːtʃɪŋ ˈɛnɪˌweɪ ˈraɪt/

299
00:15:29,674 --> 00:15:32,021
Man, she's gonna cry.
/ˈmæn ʃiːz ˌɡənə ˈkraɪ/

300
00:15:33,400 --> 00:15:36,327
It's the law of love, chunk.
/ɪts ðə ˈlɔː ʌv ˈlʌv ˈtʃʌŋk/

301
00:15:36,858 --> 00:15:38,586
Thanks, Lil.
/ˈθæŋks ˈlɪl/

302
00:15:39,253 --> 00:15:43,653
So, the next night, I took Natalie out to dinner... to do the mature thing.
/ˈsoʊ ðə ˈnɛkst ˈnaɪt aɪ ˈtʊk ˈnæɾɐli ˈaʊt tə ˈdɪnɚ tə ˈduː ðə məˈtʃʊr ˈθɪŋ/

303
00:15:44,173 --> 00:15:46,893
Look, uh, Natalie, there's something I have to say.
/ˈlʊk ˈʌ ˈnæɾɐli ðɛrz ˈsʌmθɪŋ aɪ hæv tə ˈseɪ/

304
00:15:46,893 --> 00:15:48,676
Oh, wait, wait.
/ˈoʊ ˈweɪt ˈweɪt/
There's something I have to say first.
/ðɛrz ˈsʌmθɪŋ aɪ hæv tə ˈseɪ ˈfɜːst/

305
00:15:48,676 --> 00:15:53,883
Today, at work, I had not one, not two, but three birthday cakes.
/təˈdeɪ æt ˈwɜːk aɪ hæd ˌnɑːt ˈwʌn ˌnɑːt ˈtuː ˌbʌt ˈθriː ˈbɜːθdeɪ ˈkeɪks/

306
00:15:53,883 --> 00:15:56,406
So tonight, can we just skip the cake?
/ˌsoʊ təˈnaɪt kæn wiː ˈdʒʌst ˈskɪp ðə ˈkeɪk/

307
00:15:56,977 --> 00:15:58,299
Today's your birthday?
/təˈdeɪz jʊr ˈbɜːθdeɪ/

308
00:15:58,299 --> 00:16:01,006
Yeah. No, it's okay, I wasn't telling anyone about it.
/ˈjɛh ˈnoʊ ɪts oʊˈkeɪ aɪ ˈwʌzn̩t ˈtɛlɪŋ ˈɛnɪˌwʌn ɐˈbaʊt ɪt/

309
00:16:01,006 --> 00:16:02,979
Today's your birthday!
/təˈdeɪz jʊr ˈbɜːθdeɪ/

310
00:16:02,979 --> 00:16:04,321
I...
/ˈaɪ/

311
00:16:06,324 --> 00:16:07,978
I didn't get you anything.
/aɪ ˈdɪdnt ɡɛt juː ˈɛnɪˌθɪŋ/

312
00:16:07,978 --> 00:16:09,590
Oh, it's okay.
/ˈoʊ ɪts oʊˈkeɪ/

313
00:16:10,270 --> 00:16:12,886
You know, you've already given me the bt present of all.
/juː ˈnoʊ juːv ɔˌːlrɛdi ˈɡɪvən ˌmiː ðə ˌbiˈːtiː ˈprɛzənt ʌv ˈɔːl/

314
00:16:14,300 --> 00:16:16,844
I can trust again.
/aɪ kæn ˈtrʌst ɐˈɡɛn/

315
00:16:19,296 --> 00:16:20,549
You're welcome.
/jʊr ˈwɛlkʌm/

316
00:16:26,018 --> 00:16:27,863
Oh, sir, much more wine.
/ˈoʊ ˈsɜː ˈmʌtʃ ˈmoːr ˈwaɪn/

317
00:16:34,800 --> 00:16:39,147
Henry, as New York's oldest hansom cab driver, you've seen quite a lot.
/ˈhɛnri æz ˈnuː ˈjɔːrks ˈoʊldəst ˈhænsəm ˈkæb ˈdraɪvɚ juːv ˈsiːn ˈkwaɪt ɐ ˈlɑːt/

318
00:16:39,147 --> 00:16:43,518
In your past 60 years on the job, what is your most exciting memory?
/ɪn jʊr ˈpæst ˈsɪksti ˈjɪrz ɑːnðə ˈdʒɑːb ˌwʌt ɪz jʊr ˈmoʊst ɛˈksaɪɾɪŋ ˈmɛmɚri/

319
00:16:44,258 --> 00:16:47,043
- Well...
- Ah, this is it.

320
00:16:47,043 --> 00:16:48,700
Oh, boy, here we go.
/ˈoʊ ˈbɔɪ ˈhɪr wiː ˈɡoʊ/

321
00:16:48,700 --> 00:16:51,261
Everyone, everyone, if I may direct your attention to the television.
/ˈɛvrɪˌwʌn ˈɛvrɪˌwʌn ɪf aɪ ˈmeɪ ˈdɚrɛkt jʊr ɐˈtɛnʃən tə ðə ˈtɛlɪˌvɪʒən/

322
00:16:51,261 --> 00:16:53,526
You are about to see something amazing.
/juː ɑːr ɐˌbaʊt tə ˈsiː ˈsʌmθɪŋ ɐˈmeɪzɪŋ/

323
00:16:53,526 --> 00:17:01,756
And then, in '72, Mickey Mantle rode my cab for the fourth time.
/ænd ˈðɛn ɪn ˈsɛvənti ˈtuː ˈmɪki ˈmæntəl ˈroʊd maɪ ˈkæb fɚðə ˈfoːrθ ˈtaɪm/

324
00:17:01,756 --> 00:17:04,256
Come on, baby.
/ˈkʌm ˈɑːn ˈbeɪbi/
Bring it home.
/ˈbrɪŋ ɪt ˈhoʊm/

325
00:17:04,256 --> 00:17:07,394
But the most exciting moment--
/ˌbʌt ðə ˈmoʊst ɛˈksaɪɾɪŋ ˈmoʊmənt/

326
00:17:07,394 --> 00:17:11,192
that would have to be this one, right now.
/ðæt wʊˌdhævtə biː ˈðɪˌswʌn ˈraɪt ˈnaʊ/

327
00:17:11,192 --> 00:17:12,559
What?
/ˈwʌt/

328
00:17:12,559 --> 00:17:15,736
Look at me.
/ˈlʊk æt ˌmiː/
I'm on TV.
/aɪm ˌɑːn ˌtiˈːviː/

329
00:17:15,736 --> 00:17:19,224
I never thought I'd have my story told.
/aɪ ˈnɛvɚ ˈθɔːt aɪd hæv maɪ ˈstoːri ˈtoʊld/

330
00:17:19,984 --> 00:17:23,221
Thank you, Miss Robin Trubotsky.
/ˈθæŋk juː ˈmɪs ˈrɑːbɪn truˈːbɑːtski/

331
00:17:23,221 --> 00:17:24,737
Thank you.
/ˈθæŋk juː/

332
00:17:24,737 --> 00:17:28,787
And right then, Aunt Robin realized how important her job truly was.
/ænd ˈraɪt ˈðɛn ˈænt ˈrɑːbɪn ˈriːəlaɪzd ˌhaʊ ɪˈmpoːrtənt hɜː ˈdʒɑːb ˈtruːli wʌz/

333
00:17:28,787 --> 00:17:31,504
It's an honor to tell your story, Henry.
/ɪts ɐn ˈɑːnɚ tə ˈtɛl jʊr ˈstoːri ˈhɛnri/

334
00:17:32,385 --> 00:17:36,464
You know, Metro News One may not be number one in viewership,
/juː ˈnoʊ ˈmɛtroʊ ˈnuːz ˈwʌn ˈmeɪ ˌnɑːt biː ˈnʌmbɚ ˈwʌn ɪn ˈvjuˌːɚʃɪp/

335
00:17:36,464 --> 00:17:40,432
but this reporter takes pride in...
/ˌbʌt ðɪs rɪˈpoːrɾɚ ˈteɪks ˈpraɪd ˈɪn/
Whoa! Oh...!
/ˈwoʊ ˈoʊ ˈɛkskləˌmeɪʃən/

336
00:17:40,432 --> 00:17:43,795
Oh, my God, I'm covered in horse crap!
/ˈoʊ maɪ ˈɡɑːd aɪm ˈkʌvɚd ɪn ˈhɔːrs ˈkræp/

337
00:17:44,707 --> 00:17:46,861
Oh, my God, it's in my hair.
/ˈoʊ maɪ ˈɡɑːd ɪts ɪn maɪ ˈhɛr/

338
00:17:46,861 --> 00:17:50,087
- You planned that?
- No, Marshall.

339
00:17:50,500 --> 00:17:52,800
That was beyond my wildest dreams.
/ðæt wʌz bɪˌjɑːnd maɪ ˈwaɪldəst ˈdriːmz/

340
00:17:54,422 --> 00:17:56,566
So, if you ever come to Alabama,
/ˈsoʊ ɪf juː ˈɛvɚ ˈkʌm tʊ ˌæləˈbæmə/

341
00:17:56,566 --> 00:17:59,432
my mom throws the huge crawfish boils,
/maɪ ˈmɑːm ˈθroʊz ðə ˈhjuːdʒ ˈkrɔːfɪʃ ˈbɔɪlz/

342
00:17:59,432 --> 00:18:01,998
and she's just dying to meet you, by the way.
/ænd ʃiːz ˈdʒʌst ˈdaɪɪŋ tə ˈmiːt juː baɪ ðə ˈweɪ/

343
00:18:01,998 --> 00:18:05,465
Look, Natalie, there's something I have to say, and, uh, there's no good way to say it.
/ˈlʊk ˈnæɾɐli ðɛrz ˈsʌmθɪŋ aɪ hæv tə ˈseɪ ˈænd ˈʌ ðɛrz ˈnoʊ ˈɡʊd ˈweɪ tə ˈseɪ ɪt/

344
00:18:06,543 --> 00:18:08,036
I want to break up.
/aɪ ˈwɑːnt tə ˈbreɪk ˈʌp/

345
00:18:09,156 --> 00:18:10,910
I don't think you're the one for me.
/aɪ ˈdoʊnt ˈθɪŋk jʊr ðə ˈwʌn fɔːr ˌmiː/

346
00:18:11,531 --> 00:18:15,038
I don't want to waste your time, because I really like you.
/aɪ ˈdoʊnt ˈwɑːnt tə ˈweɪst jʊr ˈtaɪm bɪˈkʌz aɪ ˈriəli ˈlaɪk juː/

347
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:20,645
I want to do right by you, and I think the best way for me to do that is just to be honest.
/aɪ ˈwɑːnt tə ˈduː ˈraɪt baɪ juː ænd aɪ ˈθɪŋk ðə ˈbɛst ˈweɪ fɔːr ˌmiː tə ˈduː ðæt ɪz ˈdʒʌst təbi ˈɑːnɪst/

348
00:18:20,645 --> 00:18:22,478
I'm sorry.
/aɪm ˈsɔːri/

349
00:18:25,300 --> 00:18:26,961
Oh, God, just let it out.
/ˈoʊ ˈɡɑːd ˈdʒʌst ˈlɛt ɪɾ ˈaʊt/

350
00:18:27,571 --> 00:18:30,131
They're only tears.
/ðeɪɚr ˈoʊnli ˈtɪrz/

351
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:37,308
I'm not the one for you?!
/aɪm ˌnɑːt ðə ˈwʌn fɔːr juː/

352
00:18:37,308 --> 00:18:39,704
I'm sorry, I just... I-I-I thought the mature thing to do...
/aɪm ˈsɔːri aɪ ˈdʒʌst aɪaɪaɪ ˈθɔːt ðə məˈtʃʊr ˈθɪŋ tə ˈduː/

353
00:18:39,704 --> 00:18:41,166
- It's my birthday!
- Yes, I know.

354
00:18:41,166 --> 00:18:41,927
I didn't realize...
/aɪ ˈdɪdnt ˈriːəlaɪz/

355
00:18:41,927 --> 00:18:45,985
It's my birthday, and you're telling me I'm not the one for you?!
/ɪts maɪ ˈbɜːθdeɪ ænd jʊr ˈtɛlɪŋ ˌmiː aɪm ˌnɑːt ðə ˈwʌn fɔːr juː/

356
00:18:45,985 --> 00:18:48,881
It's really not such a big deal.
/ɪts ˈriəli ˌnɑːt ˈsʌtʃ ɐ ˈbɪɡ ˈdiːl/
I mean, the odds--
/aɪ ˈmiːn ðɪ ˈɑːdz/

357
00:18:48,881 --> 00:18:50,826
It's like you lost the lottery.
/ɪts ˈlaɪk juː ˈlɔst ðə ˈlɑːɾɚri/

358
00:18:50,826 --> 00:18:53,111
Oh, so dating you is like winning the lottery?!
/ˈoʊ ˌsoʊ ˈdeɪɾɪŋ juː ɪz ˈlaɪk ˈwɪnɪŋ ðə ˈlɑːɾɚri/

359
00:18:53,111 --> 00:18:54,479
No, no, no, no, I didn't mean that.
/ˈnoʊ ˈnoʊ ˈnoʊ ˈnoʊ aɪ ˈdɪdnt ˈmiːn ˈðæt/

360
00:18:54,479 --> 00:18:58,633
- Okay, so what's the problem?!
- I... I... I can't explain it.

361
00:18:58,633 --> 00:19:01,469
- Try!
- It's... ineffable.

362
00:19:01,469 --> 00:19:04,359
I'm not effable?
/aɪm ˌnɑːt ˈɛfəbəl/

363
00:19:04,359 --> 00:19:08,077
No, no, no, no. "Ineffable."
/ˈnoʊ ˈnoʊ ˈnoʊ ˈnoʊ ɪˈnɛfəbəl/
Ineffable means it can't be explained.
/ɪˈnɛfəbəl ˈmiːnz ɪt ˈkænt biː ɛˈkspleɪnd/

364
00:19:08,077 --> 00:19:10,598
- Oh, so I'm stupid?
- Oh, God, what's going on?

365
00:19:10,598 --> 00:19:17,020
Okay, what's going on is you broke my heart over my answering machine on my birthday,
/oʊˈkeɪ ˌwʌts ˌɡoʊɪŋ ˌɑːn ɪz juː ˈbroʊk maɪ ˈhɑːrt ˌoʊvɚ maɪ ˈænsɚrɪŋ məˈʃiːn ˌɑːn maɪ ˈbɜːθdeɪ/

366
00:19:17,020 --> 00:19:19,936
waited three years for me to get over you,
/ˈweɪɾᵻd ˈθriː ˈjɪrz fɔːr ˌmiː tə ɡɛt ˈoʊvɚ juː/

367
00:19:19,936 --> 00:19:22,382
tracked me down, begged me to go out with you again,
/ˈtrækt ˌmiː ˈdaʊn ˈbɛɡd ˌmiː tə ˌɡoʊ ˈaʊt wɪð juː ɐˈɡɛn/

368
00:19:22,382 --> 00:19:27,292
only so you could dump me three weeks later, again, on my birthday!
/ˈoʊnli ˌsoʊ juː kʊd ˈdʌmp ˌmiː ˈθriː ˈwiːks ˈleɪɾɚ ɐˈɡɛn ˌɑːn maɪ ˈbɜːθdeɪ/

369
00:19:27,292 --> 00:19:29,767
No, it's-it's-it's not like that.
/ˈnoʊ ɪtsɪtsɪts ˌnɑːt ˈlaɪk ˈðæt/

370
00:19:29,767 --> 00:19:32,277
- I'm just... it's-it's-it's...
- What?!

371
00:19:32,277 --> 00:19:35,676
I'm just, like, so busy right now.
/aɪm ˈdʒʌst ˈlaɪk ˌsoʊ ˈbɪzi ˈraɪt ˈnaʊ/

372
00:19:36,400 --> 00:19:38,157
Remember when Natalie said...
/rɪˈmɛmbɚ wɛn ˈnæɾɐli ˈsɛd/

373
00:19:38,157 --> 00:19:41,037
I have my Krav Maga class in half an hour.
/aɪ hæv maɪ ˈkræv ˈmɑːɡə ˈklæs ɪn ˈhæf ɐn ˈaɪʊr/

374
00:19:41,037 --> 00:19:43,854
Turns out Krav Maga is not a kind of yoga.
/ˈtɜːnz ˈaʊt ˈkræv ˈmɑːɡə ɪz ˌnɑːɾə ˈkaɪnd ʌv ˈjoʊɡə/

375
00:19:43,854 --> 00:19:47,478
It's a form of guerilla street fighting developed by the Israeli army.
/ɪts ɐ ˈfɔːrm ʌv ɡɛˈrɪlə ˈstriːt ˈfaɪɾɪŋ dɪˈvɛləpt baɪ ðɪ ɪˈzreɪli ˈɑːrmi/

376
00:19:51,948 --> 00:19:55,365
This is compliments of those two gentlemen at the bar.
/ðɪs ɪz ˈkɑːmplɪmənts ʌv ðoʊz ˈtuː ˈdʒɛntəlmən æt ðə ˈbɑːr/

377
00:19:56,005 --> 00:19:57,669
My knee!
/maɪ ˈniː/

378
00:19:57,669 --> 00:20:00,114
It's in my hair!
/ɪts ɪn maɪ ˈhɛr/

379
00:20:02,207 --> 00:20:04,732
But isn't nice to know people are watching?
/ˌbʌt ˌɪzənt ˈnaɪs tə ˈnoʊ ˈpiːpəl ɑːr ˈwɑːtʃɪŋ/

380
00:20:08,482 --> 00:20:10,838
Oh, my God.
/ˈoʊ maɪ ˈɡɑːd/
Are you all right?
/ɑːr juː ˈɔːl ˈraɪt/

381
00:20:10,838 --> 00:20:12,570
What happened to you?
/ˌwʌt ˈhæpənd tə juː/

382
00:20:13,141 --> 00:20:14,743
I told the truth.
/aɪ ˈtoʊld ðə ˈtruːθ/

383
00:20:14,743 --> 00:20:18,011
Turns out the truth has a mean roundhouse kick.
/ˈtɜːnz ˈaʊt ðə ˈtruːθ hɐz ɐ ˈmiːn ˈraʊndhaʊs ˈkɪk/

384
00:20:18,011 --> 00:20:19,374
Oh, man.
/ˈoʊ ˈmæn/

385
00:20:19,374 --> 00:20:21,157
Oh, well, you did the right thing.
/ˈoʊ ˈwɛl juː ˈdɪd ðə ˈraɪt ˈθɪŋ/

386
00:20:21,157 --> 00:20:23,622
- I'm proud of you.
- I'm bleeding internally.

387
00:20:24,184 --> 00:20:26,072
Hey, Ted, you know what always picks me up when I'm down?
/ˈheɪ ˈtɛd juː ˈnoʊ wʌt ˈɔːlweɪz ˈpɪks ˌmiː ˌʌp wɛn aɪm ˈdaʊn/

388
00:20:26,072 --> 00:20:28,888
Other people's misfortune.
/ˈʌðɚ ˈpiːpəlz mɪˈsfɔːrtʃən/
You missed something so amazing.
/juː ˈmɪst ˈsʌmθɪŋ ˌsoʊ ɐˈmeɪzɪŋ/

389
00:20:28,888 --> 00:20:32,093
Please, can we just have one person in this whole bar who didn't see it?
/ˈpliːz kæn wiː ˈdʒʌst hæv ˈwʌn ˈpɜːsən ɪn ðɪs ˈhoʊl ˈbɑːr ˌhuː ˈdɪdnt ˈsiː ɪt/

390
00:20:32,093 --> 00:20:33,144
Fine.
/ˈfaɪn/

391
00:20:33,927 --> 00:20:35,122
Are you okay?
/ɑːr juː oʊˈkeɪ/

392
00:20:35,745 --> 00:20:38,191
I really thought I was doing it the good way this time.
/aɪ ˈriəli ˈθɔːt aɪ wʌz ˌduːɪŋ ɪt ðə ˈɡʊd ˈweɪ ðɪs ˈtaɪm/

393
00:20:38,191 --> 00:20:40,054
I guess there is no good way.
/aɪ ˈɡɛs ðɛr ɪz ˈnoʊ ˈɡʊd ˈweɪ/

394
00:20:40,503 --> 00:20:43,189
Sometimes, no matter how hard you try to do the right thing,
/ˈsʌmtaɪmz ˈnoʊ ˈmæɾɚ ˌhaʊ ˈhɑːrd juː ˈtraɪ tə ˈduː ðə ˈraɪt ˈθɪŋ/

395
00:20:43,189 --> 00:20:45,092
you just end up flat on your back,
/juː ˈdʒʌst ˈɛnd ˌʌp ˈflæt ˌɑːn jʊr ˈbæk/

396
00:20:45,092 --> 00:20:47,831
